@startuml
title Smart Campus Study Room Booking - Domain Class Diagram

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class Student {
  - studentId: String
  - name: String

  + viewAvailability(startTime: DateTime, duration: Duration)
  + bookRoom(room: Room, startTime: DateTime, duration: Duration): Booking
  + cancelBooking(booking: Booking)
}

class Room {
  - roomId: String
  - name: String
  - blocked: Boolean

  + isAvailable(startTime: DateTime, duration: Duration): Boolean
  + block()
  + unblock()
}

class Booking {
  - bookingId: String
  - startTime: DateTime
  - endTime: DateTime
  - status: BookingStatus

  + getDuration(): Duration
  + overlaps(other: Booking): Boolean
  + cancel()
  + generateConfirmation()
}

class Administrator {
  - administratorId: String
  - name: String

  + blockRoom(room: Room)
  + unblockRoom(room: Room)
  + reviewUsage(startDate: Date, endDate: Date)
}

enum BookingStatus {
  ACTIVE
  CANCELLED
}

' Persistent domain associations
Student "1" -- "0..*" Booking : makes >
Room "1" -- "0..*" Booking : reserved for >

' Behavioural dependencies rather than persistent ownership
Administrator ..> Room : manages status
Administrator ..> Booking : reviews usage

note right of Booking
R1:
startTime must be in the future.
Duration must be > 0 and <= 2 hours.

R2:
ACTIVE bookings for the same Room
must not overlap.

Touching bookings are allowed:
endTime = another startTime
is not an overlap.
end note

note right of Room
R3:
A blocked Room cannot accept
a new Booking.

Blocking does not automatically
cancel existing Bookings.
end note

note bottom of Booking
R4 / US-04:
A successful booking produces
confirmation.

A successful cancellation also
produces confirmation.

Confirmation is represented here
as behaviour rather than as a
separate persistent domain class.
end note

note bottom of Administrator
Usage review is based on Booking
information for a selected period.
end note

legend bottom
Assumptions:
1. Each Booking is made by exactly one Student.
2. Each Booking reserves exactly one Room.
3. A Student may have zero or many Bookings.
4. A Room may have zero or many Bookings over time.
5. Cancelled bookings remain represented using BookingStatus
   but do not count as active bookings for overlap checking.
6. Room.blocked represents the current blocked/unblocked state.
7. Availability is derived from Room.blocked and existing
   ACTIVE Bookings; it is not stored as a separate object.
8. Confirmation is an outcome of successful booking or
   cancellation and is not assumed to be a persistent entity.
9. Usage is derived from Booking data over the selected period,
   so no separate Usage or Report class is assumed.
10. No inheritance or composition is introduced because the
    approved requirements do not establish such relationships.
endlegend

@enduml
